{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Every soul that eats a carcass.</b> It says <b>every soul</b> to include all those enumerated above (Leviticus 17:10) — eight categories, as we explained — and it mentioned two comprehensive categories: the native-born and the stranger. And it was precise in saying <b>among the native-born and among the stranger</b> — meaning, everyone included in the native-born and everyone included in the stranger."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:59.553530930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}